      "ts": 1795197576000,
      "fullText": "EXCLUSIVE Technology Startups EXCLUSIVE Musk Ally Akis Joins Board of DOGE Alumni Firm After New Round Facebook X LinkedIn Email Link Gift Expand Elon Musk Photographer: Kent Nishimura/AFP/Getty Images Facebook X LinkedIn Email Link Gift Gift this article Contact us: Provide news feedback or report an error Confidential tip? Send a tip to our reporters Site feedback: Take our Survey New Window Facebook X LinkedIn Email Link Gift By Carmen Arroyo November 20, 2026 at 5:59 PM UTC Bookmark Save Takeaways by Bloomberg AI Elon Musk ally Baris Akis is joining the board of Special, a company led by two former staffers from the Department of Government Efficiency, Musk’s controversial government cost-cutting project. The firm, which seeks to buy businesses and cut waste by implementing artificial intelligence, raised its latest funding at a valuation of $250 million, a person familiar with the matter said. Akis’ investment firm Human Capital led the round, the person added, declining to be identified as the details are private."
